  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want an MP thread delete to send nothing if my login changes between the session check and the POST, so that a delete never leaves with another login's cookies.\n\n### Scope\n- `DeletePrivateMessageFlow` (#441, merged as b23bd6e) checks the identity, then makes one actor hop before the POST. CodeRabbit's Low note: a login adopted in that hop sends the old token with the new cookies. HFR refuses that combination (`W64x`), so nothing is deleted today, but the fence belongs in the session's own turn.\n- Use `PostingSession.send(since:)` from #412 (LOT-054), as the poll vote does: identity, `loginGeneration`, token and request in one turn of the session actor. A changed login gives `loginChanged`, and nothing is sent.\n- Test: the delete fails with `loginChanged` when a login lands between the check and the send. The test must fail without the fence, and the write must never reach HFR (loopback-only session, #314).\n\n### Blocked by\n- #412 (LOT-054), which brings `send(since:)`.\n\n### Decision\nOperator, 2026-11-02: accept #441's Low note, merge it, and close the hop in this follow-up.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
